  "items": [
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-095",
      "sourceNumber": "95",
      "contentHash": "23bc42f2bb7b8aeb",
      "title": "共通部分と和集合",
      "sourcePage": 26,
      "sourceLevel": "STEP A",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "intersection-and-union",
      "problemText": "次の各場合について、A∩B と A∪B を求めよ。\n(1) A={1,3,5,7}, B={0,1,2,3}\n(2) A={2,3,5,8}, B={1,4,6}\n(3) A={x｜−3≦x≦2}, B={x｜−1<x<4}（xは実数）\n(4) A={n｜nは18の正の約数}, B={n｜nは27の正の約数}\n(5) A={2n+1｜0≦n≦6}, B={3n+1｜0≦n≦4}（nは整数）",
      "miniGuide": "∩は両方、∪は少なくとも一方。区間では端点を含むかも確認する。",
      "answer": "(1) ∩={1,3}, ∪={0,1,2,3,5,7}\n(2) ∩=∅, ∪={1,2,3,4,5,6,8}\n(3) ∩={x｜−1<x≦2}, ∪={x｜−3≦x<4}\n(4) ∩={1,3,9}, ∪={1,2,3,6,9,18,27}\n(5) ∩={1,7,13}, ∪={1,3,4,5,7,9,10,11,13}",
      "keyPoint": "区間の和集合・共通部分では境界の不等号を写し間違えない。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    },
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-096",
      "sourceNumber": "96",
      "contentHash": "fd122a57d6955005",
      "title": "3集合の演算",
      "sourcePage": 26,
      "sourceLevel": "STEP A",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "compound-set-operations",
      "problemText": "A={n｜nは16の正の約数}、B={n｜nは24の正の約数}、C={n｜nは8以下の自然数} とする。次を求めよ。\n(1) A∩B∩C　(2) A∪B∪C",
      "miniGuide": "A、B、Cを先に要素表示する。3つすべてに入るものと、どれかに入るものを分ける。",
      "answer": "(1) {1,2,4,8}\n(2) {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,16,24}",
      "keyPoint": "Cに5と7が含まれるため、和集合にも入る。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    },
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-097",
      "sourceNumber": "97",
      "contentHash": "f349245cb1f840c4",
      "title": "補集合を含む演算",
      "sourcePage": 26,
      "sourceLevel": "STEP A",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "compound-set-operations",
      "problemText": "U={x｜1≦x≦10、xは整数} を全体集合とし、A={1,2,3,5,7}、B={2,3,8,10} とする。次を求めよ。\n(1) Ā　(2) B̄　(3) (A∩B)ᶜ　(4) A∪B̄\n(5) Ā∩B̄　(6) (A∪B)ᶜ　(7) Ā∩B　(8) Ā∪B",
      "miniGuide": "補集合は必ずUを基準にする。(3)(6)は先に括弧内を求める。",
      "answer": "(1) {4,6,8,9,10}\n(2) {1,4,5,6,7,9}\n(3) {1,4,5,6,7,8,9,10}\n(4) {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9}\n(5) {4,6,9}\n(6) {4,6,9}\n(7) {8,10}\n(8) {2,3,4,6,8,9,10}",
      "keyPoint": "(5)と(6)はド・モルガンの法則で一致する。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    },
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-099",
      "sourceNumber": "99",
      "contentHash": "20c18e81c730ddf8",
      "title": "3集合と補集合",
      "sourcePage": 26,
      "sourceLevel": "STEP B",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "compound-set-operations",
      "problemText": "U={1,2,…,10}、A={1,2,3,4,8}、B={3,4,5,6}、C={2,3,6,7} とする。次を求めよ。\n(1) A∩B∩C　(2) A∪B∪C　(3) A∩B∩C̄\n(4) Ā∩B∩C̄　(5) (A∩B∩C)ᶜ　(6) (A∪C)∩B̄",
      "miniGuide": "一度に処理せず、括弧・共通部分・補集合を左から小さく計算する。",
      "answer": "(1) {3}\n(2) {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}\n(3) {4}\n(4) {5}\n(5) {1,2,4,5,6,7,8,9,10}\n(6) {1,2,7,8}",
      "keyPoint": "(5)の横線は3集合全体にかかる。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    },
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-100",
      "sourceNumber": "100",
      "contentHash": "732d46343c62148c",
      "title": "共通部分から定数を決定",
      "sourcePage": 26,
      "sourceLevel": "STEP B",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "compound-set-operations",
      "problemText": "A={1,3,3a−2}、B={−5,a+2,a²−2a+1}、A∩B={1,4} のとき、定数aの値とA∪Bを求めよ。",
      "miniGuide": "4がAに入る条件とBに入る条件を照合し、1も共通になるか、余計な共通要素が出ないかを確認する。",
      "answer": "a=2、A∪B={−5,1,3,4}",
      "keyPoint": "a=2のときA={1,3,4}、B={−5,4,1}。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    },
    {
      "sourceQuestionId": "math-i-4step-set-ex-a08",
      "sourceNumber": "演習A-8",
      "contentHash": "cf2a249311376bd7",
      "title": "集合と定数",
      "sourcePage": 32,
      "sourceLevel": "演習問題A",
      "majorUnit": "sets-and-logic",
      "subcategory": "set-operations",
      "problemType": "compound-set-operations",
      "problemText": "A={2,10,|a−2|}、B={3,a−3,a+3,2a} について、A∩B={2,3} のとき、aの値とA∪Bを求めよ。",
      "miniGuide": "3がAに入る条件からaの候補を出し、2がBに入るか、余計な共通要素がないかで絞る。",
      "answer": "a=−1、A∪B={−4,−2,2,3,10}",
      "keyPoint": "a=5では10も共通要素になってしまう。",
      "authoringStatus": "source-ready"
    }
  ]
